    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Provides (year, month, dayOfMonth) triples that should all be rejected by {@link PaxDate#of} with a {@link DateTimeException}. Pax calendar rules (relevant here): - Non-leap years have 13 months of 28 days each (months 1–13). - Leap years (e.g. 1900: last two digits \"00\", not divisible by 400) have 14 months: months 1–12 with 28 days, month 13 (the \"Pax\" leap-month) with 7 days, and month 14 with 28 days. - 1898 is NOT a leap year (last two digits 98, not divisible by 6 or 99). - 1900 IS a leap year (last two digits 00, 1900 % 400 != 0)."
   },
